# The cv release the site is built from, and the sha256 of its four assets.
#
# The trust anchor is the four digests below, in this repository. A release tag
# is not immutable: a moved tag or a replaced asset would change the build
# silently, so task content:build refuses any asset whose sha256 differs from
# the pin, and refuses an empty digest next to a set tag.
#
# CV_RELEASE_TAG must be a version tag, never a branch or "latest". The assets
# are downloaded from
# https://github.com/ostendorf-cloud/cv/releases/download/<tag>/<asset> with
# the asset names cv.de.json, cv.en.json, cv.de.pdf and cv.en.pdf.
#
# To bump, by hand: download the four assets of the new release, then
#   sha256sum cv.de.json cv.en.json cv.de.pdf cv.en.pdf
# and set all five values together in one commit. A cv release does not reach
# the site before that and a rebuild.
#
# All five are empty until the cv repository has published a release that
# carries the two PDFs, so a build fails loudly until they are set.
CV_RELEASE_TAG=
CV_RELEASE_SHA256_DE=
CV_RELEASE_SHA256_EN=
CV_RELEASE_SHA256_PDF_DE=
CV_RELEASE_SHA256_PDF_EN=
